  "messages": [
   {
    "role": "system",
    "content": "You build one part in a CAD kernel by calling tools. Each tool is one operation; the kernel's inspection after it comes back to you.\nLengths are {\"value\": <number>, \"unit\": \"mm\" | \"cm\" | \"m\" | \"in\"}. Sketches lie on a plane through the origin: \"top\" is XY, \"front\" is XZ, \"right\" is YZ.\nextrude and cut take a sketch id. Holes are drilled along Z from the top of the part at XY positions. Fillet and chamfer edges are named \"<feature id>:edge:<n>\".\nA document starts with new_part. Give every operation a new id. If an operation is refused or fails, read its error and correct it.\nWhen the request is done, reply with one line and call no tool."
   },
   {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "The document exists.\nThe plate is feature x, extruded 10 mm. Make it 8 mm thick by calling modify_dimension with parameter \"x.depth\"."
   },
   {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "I'll modify the extrusion depth of feature x.",
